.TH "EPX\-COUNTRIES" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-countries \- read countries, and activate or deactivate them
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx countries [flags]
epx countries [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads all countries known to the tenant, active or not (ACTIVE shows which ones the tenant uses). REGIONS lists region codes (see \fBepx regions\fR).
.PP
Its reads need no OAuth scope. Its writes require the country.country_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx countries get"
Show one country.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx countries get CODE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads all countries known to the tenant, active or not (ACTIVE shows which ones the tenant uses). REGIONS lists region codes (see \fBepx regions\fR).
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CODE, NAME, ACTIVE, REGIONS.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx countries list"
List countries.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx countries list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads all countries known to the tenant, active or not (ACTIVE shows which ones the tenant uses). REGIONS lists region codes (see \fBepx regions\fR).
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CODE, NAME, ACTIVE, REGIONS.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx countries patch"
Activate or deactivate a country.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx countries patch CODE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Activates the country CODE for the tenant (\fB\-\-active\fR) or deactivates it (\fB\-\-active=false\fR): Emporix lets a PATCH change active only. epx takes the country\(aqs metadata.version as read (\fB\-\-version\fR, as \fBepx countries get CODE \-o json\fR prints it), which the reference asks for; Emporix does not check it, so a stale version is accepted and applied. \fB\-\-file\fR gives the JSON body instead, e.g. \fB{"active": true, "metadata": {"version": 1}}\fR. An unknown CODE is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PATCH. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the country.country_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-active\fR
Activate the country, or with \fB\-\-active=false\fR deactivate it (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-version <VERSION>\fR
The VERSION of the country as read (metadata.version; required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx countries patch NL \-\-active \-\-version 1
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBepx\fR(1) for the global options, the credentials epx reads and its exit codes; https://commerce-cloud-integrations.github.io/emporix-cli/commands/countries
